---
const connectionSteps = [
  { label: 'Bob: Web2 Agent on Frely', icon: 'M8 8 4 12l4 4m8-8 4 4-4 4M14 5l-4 14' },
  { label: 'Alice: Web3 Agent identity', icon: 'M14 4h5a1 1 0 0 1 1 1v14a1 1 0 0 1-1 1h-5M4 12h11m-4-4 4 4-4 4' },
  { label: 'Offering links identity to Agent', icon: 'M9 12a3 3 0 1 0 6 0 3 3 0 0 0-6 0M12 9V5m0 10v4M9.4 10.5 5.5 8.2m9.1 5.3 3.9 2.3M9.4 13.5l-3.9 2.3m9.1-5.3 3.9-2.3M10.5 3.5a1.5 1.5 0 1 0 3 0 1.5 1.5 0 0 0-3 0m0 17a1.5 1.5 0 1 0 3 0 1.5 1.5 0 0 0-3 0M3 7.5a1.5 1.5 0 1 0 3 0 1.5 1.5 0 0 0-3 0m15 9a1.5 1.5 0 1 0 3 0 1.5 1.5 0 0 0-3 0M3 16.5a1.5 1.5 0 1 0 3 0 1.5 1.5 0 0 0-3 0m15-9a1.5 1.5 0 1 0 3 0 1.5 1.5 0 0 0-3 0' },
  { label: 'Consumer buys the Offering', icon: 'M13 3 5 14h6l-1 7 9-12h-7l1-6Z' },
];
---

<section id="creators" class="story-section creators" aria-labelledby="creators-heading" data-testid="creator-section">
  <div class="creator-heading-row" data-reveal>
    <h2 id="creators-heading" class="story-heading">Package an Agent.<br /><span>Publish an Offering.</span></h2>
    <div><p class="story-intro">A publisher can sell access to an existing Web2 Agent without owning its implementation. The Offering records the publisher, the capability, the underlying Agent reference and the sale terms.</p><a class="creator-link" href="https://github.com/FrelyHQ/frely-network" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Explore the project on GitHub<svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M6 18 18 6M6 6h12v12" /></svg></a></div>
  </div>
  <ol class="creator-path" aria-label="Create a Network Offering" data-reveal>
    {connectionSteps.map((step, index) => (
      <li style={`--node-delay: ${index * 1.5}s`}>
        {index < connectionSteps.length - 1 && <div class="creator-connection" aria-hidden="true"><span /></div>}
        <div class="creator-node" aria-hidden="true">
          <svg width="30" height="30" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d={step.icon} /></svg>
        </div>
        <div class="creator-step-copy"><span class="creator-step-number">0{index + 1}</span><p>{step.label}</p></div>
      </li>
    ))}
  </ol>
  <div class="creator-audiences" data-reveal>
    <div>
      <span class="story-label"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m16 3 5 5L9 20l-6 1 1-6L16 3ZM13 6l5 5" /></svg>For publishers</span>
      <h3>Own the Web3 sale relationship.</h3><p>Create an Offering for a capability you can resell or distribute. Your Web3 Agent owns the Offering. The underlying Agent remains a separate Web2 asset.</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <span class="story-label"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="8" cy="7" r="3" /><rect x="15" y="5" width="6" height="6" rx="1.5" /><path d="M2 20v-2a6 6 0 0 1 12 0v2m2-5h2a4 4 0 0 1 4 4v1M18 3v2" /></svg>For Agent owners</span>
      <h3>Keep the runtime and Web2 ownership.</h3><p>Frely keeps the Agent identity, runtime, access policy and Web2 billing. One Agent can support multiple Network Offerings.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
